    "created_at": "2024-02-06T17:14:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-06T17:14:40Z",
    "body": "> Drive-by: Did we already discuss \"cloneable\" vs. \"clonable\" (no \"e\")? I guess `shadowRoot.clonable` shipped some time ago, so I'm codifying that in [whatwg/whatwg.org#433](https://github.com/whatwg/whatwg.org/pull/433).\r\n\r\nIt's weirdly hard to tell what the actual \"correct\" spelling is for this word, since the discourse is corrupted by the computing references (like Java). It sounds vaguely to me like `clonable` might be the proper English. In any case, I'm really glad it looks like we don't have to rename this. 😄 ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
